/P 59 0 R
/E (PRRSV is an enveloped, single-stranded RNA virus belonging to the family Arteriviridae. It primarily targets pigs and is one of the most economically significant pathogens in global swine production. The virus exists in two major genotypes: the European leystad virus \(Type 1\) and the North American VR-2332 \(Type 2\), both of which can cause reproductive failure in sows and severe respiratory disease in pigs. PRRSV is highly mutable, which complicates vaccine development. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
