/P 64 0 R
/E (There are a lot of different causes but the main reasons are contact with infected poultry and contaminated equipment. Infected poultry are birds who are affected by disease, and within contact, the disease can spread to the chicken rapidly. This can also happen when the chickens have a direct contact contaminated with the poultry products. For example, when a chicken directly contacts with contaminated manure, litter, equipment, clothing, feed, or water, then the chicken who touched the items can be infected by the disease, which leads to the infection of the Avian influenza.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
