159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (When chickens gets infected by Avian influenza, there are different symptoms that are shown throughout their body, which are like decreased energy and appetite, having nasal discharge\(runny nose\), ruffled feathers, purple discoloration throughout the comb, wattles, and legs, having diarrhea, Incoordination or lack of coordination, and more. Sometimes, a high number of chickens may die suddenly, often with no prior signs or any symptoms. For example, if you see picture 2, you can see how the leg, which is called shank, is starting to lose color and starting to turn purple. As well as in section b, you can see the comb, the fleshy red-colored outgrowth, is also losing color with the size becoming smaller. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
